# Deny list for scripts/check-pii.mjs. Copy to `.pii-names`, which is gitignored.
#
#   cp .pii-names.example .pii-names
#
# One name per line. `#` starts a comment. Matching is case-sensitive and on word
# boundaries, so a capitalised name in prose is caught while a lowercase identifier that
# happens to contain it is not.
#
# WHY THIS FILE IS NOT THE LIST. An earlier version kept the names inline in
# check-pii.mjs, reasoning that anyone who could read the list could already read the
# repository. That stopped being true of the goal rather than the access: the history was
# rewritten specifically to remove those names, and the checker was republishing every one
# of them, permanently, in the file doing the purging.
#
# So the names live on the machines that push, and never in a commit. If you clone this
# repository the check still runs its identifier patterns and tells you, loudly, that it
# has no name list.
#
# Put first names in as well as full ones. Next to a repository about somebody's personal
# notes, a first name plus a note count is identifying.

# Colleagues, family, anyone who appears in the vault:
# Firstname
# Firstname Lastname
